  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Toutou Beach, created in 2022 at Saint-Elme, is the dog swimming area provided by the city of La Seyne-sur-Mer. According to an actu.fr article from August 2022, most of the town's beaches are off-limits to dogs, with no exception for hours or leashes.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the city, Toutou Beach is at the very end of the Saint-Elme harbour, just past the diving club. The order governing it only allows dogs on a leash, muzzled for category 2 dogs; category 1 dogs are banned. Dogs may not be made to play or run on the beach or in the water, and use of the site must not obstruct users of the neighbouring boat launch ramp. The city's page states that the area is open year-round (it is meant to last beyond the summer) and that a sign at the entrance recalls the rules. Hours are 9am-12.30pm and 2.30pm-7pm from 1 October to 31 May, then 9am-12.30pm and 3pm-8pm in summer (the Provence Méditerranée tourist office listing gives 12pm for the winter morning). During the summer season the beach is closed on Wednesdays, firework days, because it serves as a staging area and is then closed to the public. A bag dispenser and bins are provided. Guide dogs for visually impaired people may use all beaches.</p>
      <h3>Worth checking before you go</h3>
      <p>The winter morning closing time differs by half an hour between the city's page (12.30pm) and the tourist office listing (12pm), and any exceptional closures on firework evenings other than the summer Wednesday are not detailed: ask the town hall. Do not confuse it with the Saint-Elme dog beach on the Saint-Mandrier-sur-Mer side, a separate site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: don't settle on another La Seyne beach thinking "it's the same": check first, most of them are off-limits to dogs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Saint-Elme harbour and the boat launch ramp are next to the area, which lies south of the Saint-Elme nautical base.</p>
